&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis 1.47 right parenthesis left parenthesis 200 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mn>1.47</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>200</mn></mfenced></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"294\"><mn>294</mn>\n</math>. Therefore, <math alttext=\"294\"><mn>294</mn>\n</math> students are enrolled in the interior design program this year.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p>Last year, <math alttext=\"200\"><mn>200</mn>\n</math> students enrolled in an interior design program. This year, the number of students enrolled is <math alttext=\"147 percent sign\"><mn>147</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of last year&rsquo;s number. How many students are enrolled in the interior design program this year?</p>","externalid":"20029b3e-d1cb-42ea-9a4b-f926abe12665","templateid":"073eb6fa-b12a-4e21-a03d-220d6fea48b7","vaultid":"e4a5bd27-5e89-45ad-ab9b-27c04239badb","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"a24fccb2-ea15-4d8b-9e72-99105cb447e1","content":"<p><math alttext=\"247\"><mn>247</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2c31da5e-90bf-4adc-b2be-65ab3893f403","content":"<p><math alttext=\"294\"><mn>294</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"bbf3b92a-9488-4263-9e3a-5afa7d5b66ef","content":"<p><math alttext=\"347\"><mn>347</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"9a8f849d-7091-4d5f-827b-8b249c142b64","content":"<p><math alttext=\"394\"><mn>394</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1691007959831,"updateDate":1691007959831}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959831, 1691007959831),
    ($SATQ$194ae3b1$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$029360-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Percentages$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">There were approximately 113,000&nbsp;occupational therapy jobs in the United States in 2012. The Bureau of Labor Statistics has projected that this number will increase by 29% from 2012 to 2022. Of the following, which is closest to the number of occupational therapy jobs the bureau has projected for the United States in 2022?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">115,900</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">116,300</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">142,000</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">145,800</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. The decimal equivalent of 29% is 0.29. It&rsquo;s given that the 113,000 occupational therapy jobs in the United States in 2012 are projected to increase by 29% by 2022. Increasing 113,000 by 29% can be expressed as <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/194ae3b1/img_000_c2290ec8.png" alt="113,000 times, open parenthesis, 1 plus 0 point 2 9, close parenthesis"></span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/194ae3b1/img_001_c71970fc.png" alt="113,000 times 1 point 2 9"></span>. Evaluating this expression yields 145,770. The closest number is 145,800 in choice D.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from increasing 113,000 by 2,900 instead of by 29%. Choice B is incorrect and may result from increasing 113,000 by 2.9% instead of by 29%. Choice C is incorrect and may result from increasing 113,000 by 29,000 instead of by 29%.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
