</math> of these objects?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"71c402f0-1552-4909-8cc9-0cbf0263cdd0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"146 minus t\"><mrow><mn>146</mn></mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"4b6fd4d2-f288-49fc-b1b1-dd299abc3ab0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"146 plus t\"><mrow><mn>146</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"e3cec587-061a-4907-a3b8-7758429af073","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction t Over 146 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<mi>t</mi>\n\t\t<mn>146</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"49c972c8-faba-4e38-8d85-3d87cbe0a070","content":"<p><math alttext=\"146 t\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>146</mn>\n\t<mi>t</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["49c972c8-faba-4e38-8d85-3d87cbe0a070"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the total mass, in kilograms, of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> identical objects is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t"><mi>t</mi></math>. To obtain the expression <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="146 r"><mn>146</mn><mi>r</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> is multiplied by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="146"><mn>146</mn></math>. Therefore, to find the total mass, in kilograms, of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="146 r"><mn>146</mn><mi>r</mi></math> of these objects, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t"><mi>t</mi></math> must also be multiplied by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="146"><mn>146</mn></math>. The result of multiplying&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t"><mi>t</mi></math> by&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="146"><mn>146</mn></math> is the expression <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="146 t"><mn>146</mn><mi>t</mi></math>. Therefore, the total mass, in kilograms, of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="146 r"><mn>146</mn><mi>r</mi></math> of these objects, is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="146 t"><mn>146</mn><mi>t</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
