<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"1d945139","external_id":"72a6fbc6-5106-42d1-b891-58079546b368","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"69afaf5e-4b4f-4202-9ee3-100c1f7b58b5","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The total mass, in kilograms, of <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math> identical objects is <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math>. Which expression represents the total mass, in kilograms, of <math alttext=\"146 r\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>146</mn>\n\t<mi>r</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> of these objects?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"71c402f0-1552-4909-8cc9-0cbf0263cdd0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"146 minus t\"><mrow><mn>146</mn></mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>t</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"4b6fd4d2-f288-49fc-b1b1-dd299abc3ab0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"146 plus t\"><mrow><mn>146</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"e3cec587-061a-4907-a3b8-7758429af073","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction t Over 146 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n\t<mfrac>\n\t\t<mi>t</mi>\n\t\t<mn>146</mn>\n\t</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"49c972c8-faba-4e38-8d85-3d87cbe0a070","content":"<p><math alttext=\"146 t\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>146</mn>\n\t<mi>t</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["49c972c8-faba-4e38-8d85-3d87cbe0a070"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the total mass, in kilograms, of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> identical objects is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math>. To obtain the expression <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"146 r\"><mn>146</mn><mi>r</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> is multiplied by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"146\"><mn>146</mn></math>. Therefore, to find the total mass, in kilograms, of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"146 r\"><mn>146</mn><mi>r</mi></math> of these objects, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> must also be multiplied by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"146\"><mn>146</mn></math>. The result of multiplying&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"146\"><mn>146</mn></math> is the expression <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"146 t\"><mn>146</mn><mi>t</mi></math>. Therefore, the total mass, in kilograms, of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"146 r\"><mn>146</mn><mi>r</mi></math> of these objects, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"146 t\"><mn>146</mn><mi>t</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017719,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"1d945139","skill_cd":"Q.A.","score_band_range_cd":5,"skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","createDate":1755117017719,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"","external_id":"72a6fbc6-5106-42