www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> must also be multiplied by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"146\"><mn>146</mn></math>. The result of multiplying&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"146\"><mn>146</mn></math> is the expression <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"146 t\"><mn>146</mn><mi>t</mi></math>. Therefore, the total mass, in kilograms, of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"146 r\"><mn>146</mn><mi>r</mi></math> of these objects, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"146 t\"><mn>146</mn><mi>t</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>","externalid":"72a6fbc6-5106-42d1-b891-58079546b368","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1755117017719,"updateDate":1755117017719}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017719, 1755117017719),
    ($SATQ$1dcea480$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$031679-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.E.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Probability and conditional probability$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">A bag contains a total of 60 marbles. A marble is to be chosen at random from the bag. If the probability that a blue marble will be chosen is 0.35, how many marbles in the bag are blue?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">21</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">25</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">35</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">39</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. Multiplying the number of marbles in the bag by the probability of selecting a blue marble gives the number of blue marbles in the bag. Since the bag contains a total of 60 marbles and the probability that a blue marble will be selected from the bag is 0.35, there are a total of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1dcea480/img_000_be85b008.png" alt="0 point 3 5 times 60, equals 21 "></span> blue marbles in the bag.<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from subtracting 35 from 60. Choice C is incorrect. This would be the number of blue marbles in the bag if there were a total of 100 marbles, not 60 marbles. Choice D is incorrect. This is the number of marbles in the bag that aren&rsquo;t blue.</p></p>
