cc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"1dcea480","skill_cd":"Q.E.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Probability and conditional probability","createDate":1691007959627,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"031679-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"d85d32a2-a04b-4e4e-b046-88c522060ab7","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"031679-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">A bag contains a total of 60 marbles. A marble is to be chosen at random from the bag. If the probability that a blue marble will be chosen is 0.35, how many marbles in the bag are blue?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">21</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">25</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">35</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">39</p>\n"}},"rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. Multiplying the number of marbles in the bag by the probability of selecting a blue marble gives the number of blue marbles in the bag. Since the bag contains a total of 60 marbles and the probability that a blue marble will be selected from the bag is 0.35, there are a total of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"0 point 3 5 times 60, equals 21 \"></span> blue marbles in the bag.<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from subtracting 35 from 60. Choice C is incorrect. This would be the number of blue marbles in the bag if there were a total of 100 marbles, not 60 marbles. Choice D is incorrect. This is the number of marbles in the bag that aren&rsquo;t blue.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959627,"updateDate":1691007959627,"correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale":true}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959627, 1691007959627),
    ($SATQ$1e1027a7$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$019531-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<div class="stimulus_reference "><div class="standalone_image "><img src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_004_523ba3c8.png" alt="The figure presents a scatterplot titled &ldquo;Ice Cream Sales.&rdquo; The horizontal axis is labeled &ldquo;Temperature, in degrees Celsius,&rdquo; and the integers 10 through 26, in increments of 2, are indicated. The vertical axis is labeled &ldquo;Sales, in dollars,&rdquo; and the integers 300 through 1,000, in increments of 100, are indicated. There are 12 data points in the scatterplot, and the line of best fit is drawn. The line of best fit begins slightly above the horizontal axis, and slightly to the right of the vertical axis, and slants upward and to the right. It passes through the point 12 comma 480 and the point 24 comma 880." width="208" height="137"></div></div>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The scatterplot above shows a company&rsquo;s ice cream sales <span class="italic">d</span>, in dollars, and the high temperature <span class="italic">t</span>, in degrees Celsius (&deg;C), on 12 different days. A line of best fit for the data is also shown. Which of the following could be an equation of the line of best fit?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_000_cf98c864.png\" alt=\"d equals, 0 point 0 3 t plus 402\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_001_af78ae08.png\" alt=\"d equals, 10 t plus 402\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_002_0d0f7614.png\" alt=\"d equals, 33 t plus 300\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_003_984de4ae.png\" alt=\"d equals, 33 t plus 84\"></span></span></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. On the line of best fit, <span class="italic">d</span> increases from approximately 480 to 880 between <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_005_69e41e48.png" alt="t equals 12"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_006_8ad65b19.png" alt="t equals 24"></span>. The slope of the line of best fit is the difference in <span class="italic">d</span>-values divided by the difference in <span class="italic">t</span>-values, which gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_007_51857731.png" alt="the fraction with numerator 880 minus 480, and denominator 24 minus 12, end fraction, equals, the fraction 400 over 12"></span>, or approximately 33. Writing the equation of the line of best fit in slope-intercept form gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_008_59ea8a5b.png" alt="d equals, 33 t plus b"></span>, where <span class="italic">b</span> is the <span class="italic">y</span>-coordinate of the <span class="italic">y</span>-intercept. This equation is satisfied by all points on the line, so <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_009_d0908415.png" alt="d equals 480"></span> when <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_010_69e41e48.png" alt="t equals 12"></span>. Thus, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_011_65d088cc.png" alt="480 equals, 33 times 12, plus b"></span>, which is equivalent to <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_012_df184e02.png" alt="480 equals, 396 plus b"></span>. Subtracting 396 from both sides of this equation gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_013_e853a9e2.png" alt="b equals 84"></span>. Therefore, an equation for the line of best fit could be <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_014_984de4ae.png" alt="d equals, 33 t plus 84"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from an error in calculating the slope and misidentifying the <span class="italic">y</span>-coordinate of the <span class="italic">y</span>-intercept of the graph as the value of <span class="italic">d</span> at <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_015_eff2f2d1.png" alt=""></span> rather than the value of <span class="italic">d</span> at <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_016_4f17d563.png" alt="t equals 0"></span>. Choice B is incorrect and may result from using the smallest value of <span class="italic">t</span> on the graph as the slope and misidentifying the <span class="italic">y</span>-coordinate of the <span class="italic">y</span>-intercept of the graph as the value of <span class="italic">d</span> at <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_017_eff2f2d1.png" alt="t equals 10"></span> rather than the value of <span class="italic">d</span> at <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_018_4f17d563.png" alt="t equals 0"></span>. Choice C is incorrect and may result from misidentifying the <span class="italic">y</span>-coordinate of the <span class="italic">y</span>-intercept as the smallest value of <span class="italic">d</span> on the graph.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 19, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"1e1027a7","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"019531-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \"><div class=\"standalone_image \"><img src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_004_523ba3c8.png\" alt=\"The figure presents a scatterplot titled &ldquo;Ice Cream Sales.&rdquo; The horizontal axis is labeled &ldquo;Temperature, in degrees Celsius,&rdquo; and the integers 10 through 26, in increments of 2, are indicated. The vertical axis is labeled &ldquo;Sales, in dollars,&rdquo; and the integers 300 through 1,000, in increments of 100, are indicated. There are 12 data points in the scatterplot, and the line of best fit is drawn. The line of best fit begins slightly above the horizontal axis, and slightly to the right of the vertical axis, and slants upward and to the right. It passes through the point 12 comma 480 and the point 24 comma 880.\" width=\"208\" height=\"137\"></div></div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The scatterplot above shows a company&rsquo;s ice cream sales <span class=\"italic\">d</span>, in dollars, and the high temperature <span class=\"italic\">t</span>, in degrees Celsius (&deg;C), on 12 different days. A line of best fit for the data is also shown. Which of the following could be an equation of the line of best fit?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_000_cf98c864.png\" alt=\"d equals, 0 point 0 3 t plus 402\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_001_af78ae08.png\" alt=\"d equals, 10 t plus 402\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_002_0d0f7614.png\" alt=\"d equals, 33 t plus 300\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_003_984de4ae.png\" alt=\"d equals, 33 t plus 84\"></span></span></p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. On the line of best fit, <span class=\"italic\">d</span> increases from approximately 480 to 880 between <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_005_69e41e48.png\" alt=\"t equals 12\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_006_8ad65b19.png\" alt=\"t equals 24\"></span>. The slope of the line of best fit is the difference in <span class=\"italic\">d</span>-values divided by the difference in <span class=\"italic\">t</span>-values, which gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_007_51857731.png\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator 880 minus 480, and denominator 24 minus 12, end fraction, equals, the fraction 400 over 12\"></span>, or approximately 33. Writing the equation of the line of best fit in slope-intercept form gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_008_59ea8a5b.png\" alt=\"d equals, 33 t plus b\"></span>, where <span class=\"italic\">b</span> is the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate of the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept. This equation is satisfied by all points on the line, so <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_009_d0908415.png\" alt=\"d equals 480\"></span> when <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_010_69e41e48.png\" alt=\"t equals 12\"></span>. Thus, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_011_65d088cc.png\" alt=\"480 equals, 33 times 12, plus b\"></span>, which is equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_012_df184e02.png\" alt=\"480 equals, 396 plus b\"></span>. Subtracting 396 from both sides of this equation gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_013_e853a9e2.png\" alt=\"b equals 84\"></span>. Therefore, an equation for the line of best fit could be <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_014_984de4ae.png\" alt=\"d equals, 33 t plus 84\"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from an error in calculating the slope and misidentifying the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate of the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept of the graph as the value of <span class=\"italic\">d</span> at <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_015_eff2f2d1.png\" alt=\"\"></span> rather than the value of <span class=\"italic\">d</span> at <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_016_4f17d563.png\" alt=\"t equals 0\"></span>. Choice B is incorrect and may result from using the smallest value of <span class=\"italic\">t</span> on the graph as the slope and misidentifying the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate of the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept of the graph as the value of <span class=\"italic\">d</span> at <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_017_eff2f2d1.png\" alt=\"t equals 10\"></span> rather than the value of <span class=\"italic\">d</span> at <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e1027a7/img_018_4f17d563.png\" alt=\"t equals 0\"></span>. Choice C is incorrect and may result from misidentifying the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate of the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept as the smallest value of <span class=\"italic\">d</span> on the graph.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":19,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959615,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"1e1027a7","skill_cd":"Q.D.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","createDate":1691007959615,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"019531-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"5396cb18-1a0d-4138-9146-281334b3f86a","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"019531-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \"><div class=\"standalone_image \"><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The figure presents a scatterplot titled &ldquo;Ice Cream Sales.&rdquo; The horizontal axis is labeled &ldquo;Temperature, in degrees Celsius,&rdquo; and the integers 10 through 26, in increments of 2, are indicated. The vertical axis is labeled &ldquo;Sales, in dollars,&rdquo; and the integers 300 through 1,000, in increments of 100, are indicated. There are 12 data points in the scatterplot, and the line of best fit is drawn. The line of best fit begins slightly above the horizontal axis, and slightly to the right of the vertical axis, and slants upward and to the right. It passes through the point 12 comma 480 and the point 24 comma 880.\" width=\"208\" height=\"137\"></div></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The scatterplot above shows a company&rsquo;s ice cream sales <span class=\"italic\">d</span>, in dollars, and the high temperature <span class=\"italic\">t</span>, in degrees Celsius (&deg;C), on 12 different days. A line of best fit for the data is also shown. Which of the following could be an equation of the line of best fit?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"d equals, 0 point 0 3 t plus 402\"></span></span></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"d equals, 10 t plus 402\"></span></span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"d equals, 33 t plus 300\"></span></span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"d equals, 33 t plus 84\"></span></span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"d","rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. On the line of best fit, <span class=\"italic\">d</span> increases from approximately 480 to 880 between <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"t equals 12\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"t equals 24\"></span>. The slope of the line of best fit is the difference in <span class=\"italic\">d</span>-values divided by the difference in <span class=\"italic\">t</span>-values, which gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator 880 minus 480, and denominator 24 minus 12, end fraction, equals, the fraction 400 over 12\"></span>, or approximately 33. Writing the equation of the line of best fit in slope-intercept form gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"d equals, 33 t plus b\"></span>, where <span class=\"italic\">b</span> is the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate of the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept. This equation is satisfied by all points on the line, so <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"d equals 480\"></span> when <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"t equals 12\"></span>. Thus, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"480 equals, 33 times 12, plus b\"></span>, which is equivalent to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"480 equals, 396 plus b\"></span>. Subtracting 396 from both sides of this equation gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"b equals 84\"></span>. Therefore, an equation for the line of best fit could be <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"d equals, 33 t plus 84\"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from an error in calculating the slope and misidentifying the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate of the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept of the graph as the value of <span class=\"italic\">d</span> at <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"\"></span> rather than the value of <span class=\"italic\">d</span> at <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"t equals 0\"></span>. Choice B is incorrect and may result from using the smallest value of <span class=\"italic\">t</span> on the graph as the slope and misidentifying the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate of the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept of the graph as the value of <span class=\"italic\">d</span> at <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"t equals 10\"></span> rather than the value of <span class=\"italic\">d</span> at <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"t equals 0\"></span>. Choice C is incorrect and may result from misidentifying the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate of the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept as the smallest value of <span class=\"italic\">d</span> on the graph.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959615,"updateDate":1691007959615}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959615, 1691007959615),
    ($SATQ$1e562f24$SATQ$, $SATQ$993a9eaf-5cb2-4e31-b138-e7b5002d37c5$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$dc5f4890-0250-4fe0-9c6a-9ec386a83674$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.F.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Inference from sample statistics and margin of error $SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>To estimate the proportion of a population that has a certain characteristic, a random sample was selected from the population. Based on the sample, it is estimated that the proportion of the population that has the characteristic is <math alttext="0.49"><mn>0.49</mn>
</math>, with an associated margin of error of <math alttext="0.04"><mn>0.04</mn>
</math>. Based on this estimate and margin of error, which of the following is the most appropriate conclusion about the proportion of the population that has the characteristic?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"84e8126d-bab6-44ba-9127-9cc300be1582","content":"<p>It is plausible that the proportion is between <math alttext=\"0.45\"><mn>0.45</mn>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"0.53\"><mn>0.53</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"a96b5e53-02f3-45f8-8284-e45079b1d209","content":"<p>It is plausible that the proportion is less than <math alttext=\"0.45\"><mn>0.45</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"c79b9a3b-188c-4a82-bfeb-3d20454b37f5","content":"<p>The proportion is exactly <math alttext=\"0.49\"><mn>0.49</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"5a38cfa5-5d53-4d6f-bd02-75cf4e76543f","content":"<p>It is plausible that the proportion is greater than <math alttext=\"0.53\"><mn>0.53</mn>\n</math>.</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["84e8126d-bab6-44ba-9127-9cc300be1582"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the estimate for the proportion of the population that has the characteristic is <math alttext="0.49"><mn>0.49</mn>
</math> with an associated margin of error of <math alttext="0.04"><mn>0.04</mn>
</math>. Subtracting the margin of error from the estimate and adding the margin of error to the estimate gives an interval of plausible values for the true proportion of the population that has the characteristic. Therefore, it&rsquo;s plausible that the proportion of the population that has this characteristic is between <math alttext="0.45"><mn>0.45</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="0.53"><mn>0.53</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. A value less than <math alttext="0.45"><mn>0.45</mn>
</math> is outside the interval of plausible values for the proportion of the population that has the characteristic.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. The value <math alttext="0.49"><mn>0.49</mn>
</math> is an estimate for the proportion based on this sample. However, since the margin of error for this estimate is known, the most appropriate conclusion is not that the proportion is exactly one value but instead lies in an interval of plausible values.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. A value greater than <math alttext="0.53"><mn>0.53</mn>
</math> is outside the interval of plausible values for the proportion of the population that has the characteristic.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"1e562f24","external_id":"993a9eaf-5cb2-4e31-b138-e7b5002d37c5","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"dc5f4890-0250-4fe0-9c6a-9ec386a83674","uId":"db5c21a9-cf35-4099-bd40-7fd4a6e07386","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.F.","skill_desc":"Inference from sample statistics and margin of error ","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>To estimate the proportion of a population that has a certain characteristic, a random sample was selected from the population. Based on the sample, it is estimated that the proportion of the population that has the characteristic is <math alttext=\"0.49\"><mn>0.49</mn>\n</math>, with an associated margin of error of <math alttext=\"0.04\"><mn>0.04</mn>\n</math>. Based on this estimate and margin of error, which of the following is the most appropriate conclusion about the proportion of the population that has the characteristic?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"84e8126d-bab6-44ba-9127-9cc300be1582","content":"<p>It is plausible that the proportion is between <math alttext=\"0.45\"><mn>0.45</mn>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"0.53\"><mn>0.53</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"a96b5e53-02f3-45f8-8284-e45079b1d209","content":"<p>It is plausible that the proportion is less than <math alttext=\"0.45\"><mn>0.45</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"c79b9a3b-188c-4a82-bfeb-3d20454b37f5","content":"<p>The proportion is exactly <math alttext=\"0.49\"><mn>0.49</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"5a38cfa5-5d53-4d6f-bd02-75cf4e76543f","content":"<p>It is plausible that the proportion is greater than <math alttext=\"0.53\"><mn>0.53</mn>\n</math>.</p>"}],"keys":["84e8126d-bab6-44ba-9127-9cc300be1582"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the estimate for the proportion of the population that has the characteristic is <math alttext=\"0.49\"><mn>0.49</mn>\n</math> with an associated margin of error of <math alttext=\"0.04\"><mn>0.04</mn>\n</math>. Subtracting the margin of error from the estimate and adding the margin of error to the estimate gives an interval of plausible values for the true proportion of the population that has the characteristic. Therefore, it&rsquo;s plausible that the proportion of the population that has this characteristic is between <math alttext=\"0.45\"><mn>0.45</mn>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"0.53\"><mn>0.53</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. A value less than <math alttext=\"0.45\"><mn>0.45</mn>\n</math> is outside the interval of plausible values for the proportion of the population that has the characteristic.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. The value <math alttext=\"0.49\"><mn>0.49</mn>\n</math> is an estimate for the proportion based on this sample. However, since the margin of error for this estimate is known, the most appropriate conclusion is not that the proportion is exactly one value but instead lies in an interval of plausible values.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. A value greater than <math alttext=\"0.53\"><mn>0.53</mn>\n</math> is outside the interval of plausible values for the proportion of the population that has the characteristic.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":"manifold","position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959835,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"1e562f24","skill_cd":"Q.F.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Inference from sample statistics and margin of error ","createDate":1691007959835,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":null,"external_id":"993a9eaf-5cb2-4e31-b138-e7b5002d37c5","primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"db5c21a9-cf35-4099-bd40-7fd4a6e07386","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"keys":["84e8126d-bab6-44ba-9127-9cc300be1582"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the estimate for the proportion of the population that has the characteristic is <math alttext=\"0.49\"><mn>0.49</mn>\n</math> with an associated margin of error of <math alttext=\"0.04\"><mn>0.04</mn>\n</math>. Subtracting the margin of error from the estimate and adding the margin of error to the estimate gives an interval of plausible values for the true proportion of the population that has the characteristic. Therefore, it&rsquo;s plausible that the proportion of the population that has this characteristic is between <math alttext=\"0.45\"><mn>0.45</mn>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"0.53\"><mn>0.53</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. A value less than <math alttext=\"0.45\"><mn>0.45</mn>\n</math> is outside the interval of plausible values for the proportion of the population that has the characteristic.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. The value <math alttext=\"0.49\"><mn>0.49</mn>\n</math> is an estimate for the proportion based on this sample. However, since the margin of error for this estimate is known, the most appropriate conclusion is not that the proportion is exactly one value but instead lies in an interval of plausible values.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. A value greater than <math alttext=\"0.53\"><mn>0.53</mn>\n</math> is outside the interval of plausible values for the proportion of the population that has the characteristic.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p>To estimate the proportion of a population that has a certain characteristic, a random sample was selected from the population. Based on the sample, it is estimated that the proportion of the population that has the characteristic is <math alttext=\"0.49\"><mn>0.49</mn>\n</math>, with an associated margin of error of <math alttext=\"0.04\"><mn>0.04</mn>\n</math>. Based on this estimate and margin of error, which of the following is the most appropriate conclusion about the proportion of the population that has the characteristic?</p>","externalid":"993a9eaf-5cb2-4e31-b138-e7b5002d37c5","templateid":"bb036658-b1f1-4509-a5a0-7464532f8662","vaultid":"dc5f4890-0250-4fe0-9c6a-9ec386a83674","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"84e8126d-bab6-44ba-9127-9cc300be1582","content":"<p>It is plausible that the proportion is between <math alttext=\"0.45\"><mn>0.45</mn>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"0.53\"><mn>0.53</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"a96b5e53-02f3-45f8-8284-e45079b1d209","content":"<p>It is plausible that the proportion is less than <math alttext=\"0.45\"><mn>0.45</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"c79b9a3b-188c-4a82-bfeb-3d20454b37f5","content":"<p>The proportion is exactly <math alttext=\"0.49\"><mn>0.49</mn>\n</math>.</p>"},{"id":"5a38cfa5-5d53-4d6f-bd02-75cf4e76543f","content":"<p>It is plausible that the proportion is greater than <math alttext=\"0.53\"><mn>0.53</mn>\n</math>.</p>"}],"correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1691007959835,"updateDate":1691007959835}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959835, 1691007959835),
    ($SATQ$1e8ccffd$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$00566-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$One-variable data: Distributions and measures of center and spread$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The mean score of 8 players in a basketball game was 14.5 points. If the highest individual score is removed, the mean score of the remaining 7 players becomes 12 points. What was the highest score?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p>20</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p>24</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p>32</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p>36</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. If the mean score of 8 players is 14.5, then the total of all 8 scores is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e8ccffd/img_000_cea20d5b.png" alt="14 point 5 times 8, equals 116"></span>. If the mean of 7 scores is 12, then the total of all 7 scores is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e8ccffd/img_001_6c86460d.png" alt="12 times 7, equals 84"></span>. Since the set of 7 scores was made by removing the highest score of the set of 8 scores, then the difference between the total of all 8 scores and the total of all 7 scores is equal to the removed score: <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e8ccffd/img_002_2ec3fb15.png" alt="116 minus 84, equals 32"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect because if 20 is removed from the group of 8 scores, then the mean score of the remaining 7 players is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e8ccffd/img_003_78ae14e5.png" alt="the fraction with numerator, open parenthesis, 14 point 5 times 8, close parenthesis, minus 20, and denominator 7"></span> is approximately 13.71, not 12. Choice B is incorrect because if 24 is removed from the group of 8 scores, then the mean score of the remaining 7 players is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e8ccffd/img_004_9a8e1a6d.png" alt="the fraction with numerator, open parenthesis, 14 point 5 times 8, close parenthesis, minus 24, and denominator 7"></span> is approximately 13.14, not 12. Choice D is incorrect because if 36 is removed from the group of 8 scores, then the mean score of the remaining 7 players is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e8ccffd/img_005_b39fdf8b.png" alt="the fraction with numerator, open parenthesis, 14 point 5 times 8, close parenthesis, minus 36, and denominator 7"></span> or approximately 11.43, not 12.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"1e8ccffd","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"00566-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.C.","skill_desc":"One-variable data: Distributions and measures of center and spread","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The mean score of 8 players in a basketball game was 14.5 points. If the highest individual score is removed, the mean score of the remaining 7 players becomes 12 points. What was the highest score?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p>20</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p>24</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p>32</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p>36</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. If the mean score of 8 players is 14.5, then the total of all 8 scores is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e8ccffd/img_000_cea20d5b.png\" alt=\"14 point 5 times 8, equals 116\"></span>. If the mean of 7 scores is 12, then the total of all 7 scores is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e8ccffd/img_001_6c86460d.png\" alt=\"12 times 7, equals 84\"></span>. Since the set of 7 scores was made by removing the highest score of the set of 8 scores, then the difference between the total of all 8 scores and the total of all 7 scores is equal to the removed score: <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/1e8ccffd/img_002_2ec3fb15.png\"