    ($SATQ$1fc4f47b$SATQ$, $SATQ$d1cc7727-7dd9-47c7-90eb-06fc0e9b8ce7$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.E.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Probability and conditional probability$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">At a movie theater, there are a total of <math alttext="350"><mn>350</mn>
</math> customers. Each customer is located in either theater A, theater B, or theater C. If one of these customers is selected at random, the probability of selecting a customer who is located in theater A is <math alttext="0.48"><mn>0.48</mn>
</math>, and the probability of selecting a customer who is located in theater B is <math alttext="0.24"><mn>0.24</mn>
</math>. How many customers are located in theater C?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"3cc1eb52-88c7-4c21-94ce-ddc1487e174a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"17cc66b2-711d-4ff0-8484-96b033b636c1","content":"<p><math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f4b1b418-f2f7-401a-82ff-d47dd61c30f6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"84\"><mn>84</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b7dc9f08-88f7-4b85-9b75-ff9b6d9e4092","content":"<p><math alttext=\"98\"><mn>98</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["b7dc9f08-88f7-4b85-9b75-ff9b6d9e4092"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. It&rsquo;s given that at a movie theater, there are a total of <math alttext="350"><mn>350</mn>
</math> customers and that each customer is located in either theater A, theater B, or theater C. If the probability of selecting a customer in theater A is <math alttext="0.48"><mn>0.48</mn>
</math>, then <math alttext="left parenthesis 0.48 right parenthesis left parenthesis 350 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mn>0.48</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>350</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="168"><mn>168</mn>
</math>, customers are located in theater A. If the probability of selecting a customer in theater B is <math alttext="0.24"><mn>0.24</mn>
</math>, then <math alttext="left parenthesis 0.24 right parenthesis left parenthesis 350 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mn>0.24</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>350</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="84"><mn>84</mn>
</math>, customers are located in theater B. It follows that there are <math alttext="168 plus 84"><mn>168</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>84</mn></math>, or <math alttext="252"><mn>252</mn>
</math>, customers in theater A and theater B. Therefore, there are <math alttext="350 minus 252"><mn>350</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>252</mn></math>, or <math alttext="98"><mn>98</mn>
</math>, customers in theater C.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the percent, not the number, of the customers that are located in theater C.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the number of customers that are located in theater B, not theater C.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"1fc4f47b","external_id":"d1cc7727-7dd9-47c7-90eb-06fc0e9b8ce7","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"4103d6be-3b70-4275-a1ce-82c98a6299c7","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.E.","skill_desc":"Probability and conditional probability","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">At a movie theater, there are a total of <math alttext=\"350\"><mn>350</mn>\n</math> customers. Each customer is located in either theater A, theater B, or theater C. If one of these customers is selected at random, the probability of selecting a customer who is located in theater A is <math alttext=\"0.48\"><mn>0.48</mn>\n</math>, and the probability of selecting a customer who is located in theater B is <math alttext=\"0.24\"><mn>0.24</mn>\n</math>. How many customers are located in theater C?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"3cc1eb52-88c7-4c21-94ce-ddc1487e174a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"17cc66b2-711d-4ff0-8484-96b033b636c1","content":"<p><math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f4b1b418-f2f7-401a-82ff-d47dd61c30f6","content":"<p><math alttext=\"84\"><mn>84</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b7dc9f08-88f7-4b85-9b75-ff9b6d9e4092","content":"<p><math alttext=\"98\"><mn>98</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["b7dc9f08-88f7-4b85-9b75-ff9b6d9e4092"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. It&rsquo;s given that at a movie theater, there are a total of <math alttext=\"350\"><mn>350</mn>\n</math> customers and that each customer is located in either theater A, theater B, or theater C. If the probability of sele