\n<mi>a</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>1.60</mn>\n<mi>b</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s also given that the number <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"45 percent sign\"><mn>45</mn><mo>%</mo></math> less than <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math>. Therefore, <math alttext=\"c equals left parenthesis 1 minus StartFraction 45 Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis a\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>45</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>a</mi></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"c equals left parenthesis 1 minus 0.45 right parenthesis a\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0.45</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>a</mi></math>, or <math alttext=\"c equals 0.55 a\"><mrow>\n<mi>c</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>0.55</mn>\n<mi>a</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"a equals 1.60 b\"><mrow>\n<mi>a</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>1.60</mn>\n<mi>b</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>, substituting <math alttext=\"1.60 b\"><mrow>\n<mn>1.60</mn>\n<mi>b</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"c equals 0.55 a\"><mrow>\n<mi>c</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>0.55</mn>\n<mi>a</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"c equals 0.55 left parenthesis 1.60 b right parenthesis\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.55</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>1.60</mn><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"c equals 0.88 b\"><mrow>\n<mi>c</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mn>0.88</mn>\n<mi>b</mi>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Thus, the number <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"0.88\"><mn>0.88</mn>\n</math> times the number <math alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi>\n</math>. Note that .88 and 22/25 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.&nbsp;</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"upda